Open Vanilla: the in-game GM console's feed, clean names, and a quiet World channel.

- OpenVanilla/Gm.cpp: ".wnl gm hi|roster|bugs" answers game masters (account level 2+) over WNL
  (GM / GR / GB), for the hidden GMConsole addon; anyone else gets no answer at all.
- OpenVanilla/NameFilter.cpp: slurs and obscenities are refused in character, pet and guild names
  (through ObjectMgr::IsReservedName, so create, rename, pet names and charters all check it), and a
  character that already has one is asked to rename at its next login. OpenVanilla.NameFilter = 0
  turns it off; OpenVanilla.NameFilter.Words = "a,b" adds words. Test: tests/name_filter/run.sh.
- OpenVanilla/World.cpp: the realm's random bots (RNDBOT accounts) no longer talk in World: no
  level-up, loot or small-talk lines. OpenVanilla.WorldChannel.BotChatter = 1 lets them back.

